  "label": "Emotional Suppression Stereotype",
  "description": "The meme relies on the stereotype that men are expected to suppress their emotions, especially in front of their wives. The man's strained expression is used to represent the internal struggle of holding back tears, which is a common trope in humor about men's emotional restraint. This stereotype is part of broader cultural norms about masculinity and emotional expression.",
